      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Crown Copyright © 2015. Published by Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "We describe a woman with intracranial hypotension provoked by a combination of calcified disc protrusion and chiropractic manipulation who required surgical intervention for definitive treatment. Intracranial hypotension is a rare but increasingly well recognized cause of orthostatic headache that arises due to spinal cerebrospinal fluid leakage from meningeal diverticula or dural perforations."
      },
